content.text:
Fixed. `YearPageShell` now treats an empty or whitespace-only `subheading` the same as `undefined` — no `<h2>` gets rendered:

```tsx
const hasSubheading =
    typeof subheading === 'string'
        ? subheading.trim() !== ''
        : subheading != null;
...
{hasSubheading ? (
    <Title order={2} mb="xl">{subheading}</Title>
) : null}
```

I fixed it at the shell level rather than upstream in `games/page.tsx`, since `subheading` is typed `ReactNode` and any future caller could hit the same trap — this guards all of them at once. Added two component tests (empty string, whitespace-only string) confirming no heading renders in either case; typecheck/lint/format/knip clean, and all `YearPageShell` component tests (8) plus every year-shell page test (57 across `games`/`books`/`curse`/`winners`/`table/[table]`) pass.

